 "dur": 45.0,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Gustav made square barrels. Moving one took four sailors and a song.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.616
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Progress!\" he said. Square ones stack neater. So why are real barrels fat in the middle?",
   "s": 3.816,
   "e": 7.806
  },
  {
   "text": "But Port Puddle ships 300 barrels a day. By noon, the sailors ran out of songs.",
   "s": 8.106,
   "e": 12.542
  },
  {
   "text": "Coconut, the ship's monkey, only cared about one barrel: bananas. It was at the bottom.",
   "s": 12.742,
   "e": 16.975
  },
  {
   "text": "So Gustav upgraded again: perfect tubes. \"Progress!\"",
   "s": 17.175,
   "e": 19.792
  },
  {
   "text": "A tube rolls great. Straight ahead. Straight down the pier. Straight into the sea.",
   "s": 19.912,
   "e": 23.437
  },
  {
   "text": "Forty barrels bobbed away, with Coconut surfing on the banana one.",
   "s": 23.637,
   "e": 25.909
  },
  {
   "text": "So what is the fat middle for?",
   "s": 26.109,
   "e": 27.265
  },
  {
   "text": "A fat barrel only touches the ground at its belly. One sailor can roll it, and spin it like a top.",
   "s": 27.565,
   "e": 32.506
  },
  {
   "text": "The curve is an arch. Iron hoops squeeze the boards tight, so it can't burst.",
   "s": 32.706,
   "e": 36.369
  },
  {
   "text": "Gustav brought the fat barrels back. One sailor per barrel.",
   "s": 36.769,
   "e": 39.647
  },
  {
   "text": "The other three started a band. Coconut drums the banana barrel.",
   "s": 39.847,
   "e": 43.371
  }
 ],
